WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,536
Meet the apple. Round and smooth, with a stem on top and a shadow on the table. Let's see how it becomes one convincing drawing.

2
00:00:09,536 --> 00:00:20,944
Before any line, look. A real apple is not a perfect ball. Find the little dip at the top, the lean, the fuller side. That character is what you are really drawing.

3
00:00:20,944 --> 00:00:30,552
Measure height against width with your pencil. Frame the apple with light 2H lines. These thinking lines keep everything balanced.

4
00:00:30,552 --> 00:00:39,680
One light means one highlight and one shadow side. Find the brightest spot first, then the dark band where the surface turns away.

5
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:49,840
Lay tones from light to dark with the 2B, following the round form. Blend gently with tissue, then deepen with the 3B only where you are sure.

6
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:57,456
The stem and the cast shadow on the table take the darkest accents. Small darks make everything else glow.

7
00:00:57,456 --> 00:01:04,904
Step back, compare with the real apple, and fix the one thing that matters most. Then sign your name.

8
00:01:04,904 --> 00:01:12,760
Now it is your turn. One apple, one light, your own hand. I will guide you at every step.
